# Start a Roboter-Studio program. workflow_json is a JSON object; the
# server routes on its `language` sibling — absent or empty means a
# Blockly workspace (Blockly.serialization.workspaces.save()), which is
# dispatched by handler-table key, and 'python'/'java' means a text
# program whose `files` run in the code_runner sandbox. There is no
# allowed-block-type allowlist: a block type with no key in the handler
# table is refused by name, in German, when it is reached.
string workflow_json
string workflow_id
---
bool success
string message
# Phase-2 IK pre-check warnings: each entry is a Blockly block id whose
# concrete X/Y/Z target failed a quick IK solve. Non-fatal — the
# arm-facing refusals live in workflow/handlers/ (the table floor, the
# IK reach check, the no-go-zone reroute, the velocity floor) and apply
# to every program, Blockly or text — but the React side renders a
# setWarningText() on each block so the student sees the issue before
# the arm refuses to move.
string[] unreachable_block_ids
string[] unreachable_messages
